{"name":"Hyperpop Green","hex":"#17f9a6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hyperpop","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A microgenre of music that exaggerates common traits from pop music that originated in the 2010s."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In an extreme or exaggerated pop-music style."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hyperpop"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hyperpop","blocks":[{"text":"Hyperpop is an electronic music movement and loosely defined subgenre that originated in the early 2010s in the United Kingdom. It is characterised by an exaggerated or maximalist take on 21st century popular music tropes and typically integrates pop and avant-garde sensibilities while drawing on elements commonly found in electronic, rock, hip-hop, and dance music. The origins of hyperpop are primarily traced back to the output of English musician A. G. Cook's record label and art collective PC Music, with associated artists Sophie, GFOTY, Hayden Dunham, Hannah Diamond, and Charli XCX, helping to pioneer a musical style that was later known as \"bubblegum bass\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyperpop","wikidata":"Q104695865"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/100_Gecs_-_Rock_am_Ring_2022-3255.jpg/500px-100_Gecs_-_Rock_am_Ring_2022-3255.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/100_Gecs_-_Rock_am_Ring_2022-3255.jpg/1280px-100_Gecs_-_Rock_am_Ring_2022-3255.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/100_Gecs_-_Rock_am_Ring_2022-3255.jpg/500px-100_Gecs_-_Rock_am_Ring_2022-3255.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"100 Gecs live at Rock am Ring 2022. The duo has been credited with popularizing hyperpop in the early 2020s.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A100_Gecs_-_Rock_am_Ring_2022-3255.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Sophie_and_A._G._Cook_5.jpg/500px-Sophie_and_A._G._Cook_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Sophie_and_A._G._Cook_5.jpg/500px-Sophie_and_A._G._Cook_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"British musicians Sophie (left) and A. G. Cook (right) are considered progenitors of hyperpop","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASophie_and_A._G._Cook_5.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/100_gecs.jpg/500px-100_gecs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/100_gecs.jpg/1280px-100_gecs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/100_gecs.jpg/500px-100_gecs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In 2019, the popularity of 100 Gecs and their debut album led to Spotify launching a dedicated permanent hyperpop playlist.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A100_gecs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/CharliXCXBirm291124_%28117_of_145%29_%2854180172805%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-CharliXCXBirm291124_%28117_of_145%29_%2854180172805%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/CharliXCXBirm291124_%28117_of_145%29_%2854180172805%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-CharliXCXBirm291124_%28117_of_145%29_%2854180172805%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/CharliXCXBirm291124_%28117_of_145%29_%2854180172805%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-CharliXCXBirm291124_%28117_of_145%29_%2854180172805%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charli XCX performing during the Brat Tour in November 2024","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharliXCXBirm291124_(117_of_145)_(54180172805)_(cropped).jpg"},{"